tting. It is not Bloodlines or anything like <i>Bloodlines </i>but closer to something like <b>Monkey Island</b> or other adventure game.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;You fight like a kine!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6/10 </div> </div> </div>I'm so tempted to make a comparison to this rating and the apparent grade you gave W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T22:37:12-08:00","id":1528085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528069-vampire-the-masquerade-swansong-review?p=1528084#post1528084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm so tempted to make a comparison to this rating and the apparent grade you gave W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might give the W5 book an extra half star.<br /> <br /> This?<br /> <br /> No.<br /> <br /> Frankly, I'd give this 5/10 but I really enjoyed a couple of levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T09:54:54-08:00","id":1528111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528069-vampire-the-masquerade-swansong-review?p=1528085#post1528085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I might give the W5 book an extra half star.<br /> <br /> This?<br /> <br /> No.<br /> <br /> Frankly, I'd give this 5/10 but I really enjoyed a couple of levels.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://youtu.be/F-ijHd6qtrE?t=700\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;It's called Laserblast, and Leonard Maltin gave it two and a half stars!&quot;</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T11:44:50-08:00","id":1528114,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I dislike giving numbered ratings and often debate whether they do more harm than good because it becomes the focus of a review. I listed all of my reasoning above and what I hated and loved but people become laser-(fist) focused on the arbitary number at the end.<br /> <br /> It's why Grimdark Magazine no longer does numbers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T15:45:23-08:00","id":1528130,"title":"","content":"Numerical ratings are really only as useful as the consistency of the reviewers in how they hand them out.<br /> <br /> Swansong is actually a great example of this. CT's review is pretty much consistent with every major review of the game, but it's received everything from 3.5/10 to 8/10 (or equivalents) by major reviewers. Everyone of them all agrees about 95% of what's good and what's bad about the game The numbers just reflect differing biases on how much to weigh things. The lower ratings tend to be much more critical of it's function as a game as a primary component to giving it a rating as a game, so the jank, bugs, and outdated mechanics mean very low scores as the high points are all locked behind game play. Meanwhile reviewers that value the artistry of the writing and atmosphere games create higher tend to be more forgiving of the technical execution (even of things like plot pacing, not mechanics) because - like spending hours beating a Souls-like boss by repetition-until-mastery - getting past all that obstacle has enough pay off; thus the relatively high ratings tend to cluster on that area of bias.<br /> <br /> In-depth reviewing is always more valuable than just trying to justify a rating on a scale. Good in-depth reviews let the audience know what to expect, and generally if they're going to enjoy something even if the review gives it a low rating, or hate it even if the reviewer gives it a great rating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T00:30:51-08:00","id":1528637,"title":"","content":"Having watched playthroughs, my opinion is that the Malkavian story is compelling, the Toreador story is...okay, and the Ventrue story is boring with one good scene: the scene where he Salem's Lot speech's the guy into losing his faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T15:31:18-08:00","id":1529355,"title":"","content":"Having played <i>Vampire: the Masquerade 1</i> and also <i>Coteries of New York</i>, I can't wait to play through <i>VtM: Swansong</i>, hopefully in the nearest future. From what I have seen of<i> Swansong</i>, the game is certainly a positive experience and a welcome progression of using the <i>V:tM</i> setting as a basis and inspiration for computer games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T11:25:32-07:00","id":1554426,"title":"","content":"I replayed the game and feel like the biggest issue of it is, ironically, the fact that to enjoy the entirety of the story requires you to basically have omniscience as well as a perfect build. So much of the story is hidden behind specific skill checks and choices that you miss a lot of it if you don't do it just right or with a guide.<br /> <br /> The things that come to mind are after three or four playthroughs to get every scene.<br /> <br /> SPOILERS AHEAD<br /> <br /> * Halsey is absolutely real and Leysha's sire but Richard has been screwing with her memories. He's also faked her death so everyone else thinks Halsey is dead and Leysha is hallucinating her. Which is a hat on a hat.<br /> * The surviving London Kindred are behind the Second Inquisition's attack on Boston by using Hazel and Jara Dory in order to have the Second Inquisition wipe out Boston's Kindred so they can settle there until the heat dies down back in London.<br /> * Jason Moore's daughter was probably kidnapped not by the Second Inquisition but by the London Kindred who sent one of their ghouls to eliminate him in order to clean up loose ends. There's also no way his wife and daughter aren't already dead too. Which is your first clue that the Inquisition doesn't have them because Stanford doesn't hurt humans while the SAD does but only as collateral.<br /> * Galeb's code of honor is confusing the hell out of Berel because<i> it doesn't make any sense</i>. Galeb is fanatically loyal to the Camarilla and holds humans in disdain while he hates Berel due to the fact that the latter is after massive amounts of money while never doing anything to improve the world. I think Galeb may be on the Path of Chivalry.<br /> * Berel doesn't hate Galeb but actually loves his sire but can't figure out how to please him because of the aforementioned insane contradictions.<br /> * Xu Feng is just really fucking stupid and trying to get Berel to embrace her since Galeb is taking so long.<br /> * You don't learn that Journey Atkins is Enem's current girlfriend unless you get back all of your memories at the Hartford Chantry. Also, the worst thing you can do is send her to the Anarchs because she would have been cleared if you hadn't.<br /> * The Second Inquisition has such ridiculous supervillain/HYDRA levels of base and weaponry because the British Kindred are funding it with all of the Boston Camarilla's money. The reason it falls apart after events is because it also has served its purpose.<br /> * The SAD and Inquisition don't see eye to eye due to the fact that the former see Kindred as a security issue while the latter see it as a holy war. Monsignor Stanford is the only one who can convince the two to work together and it falls apart immediately upon his death.<br /> * Cerys, one of the Anarch Barons, is also an agent of the British Kindred. Which means that betraying the Anarchs is actually the best thing for the Boston Camarilla. <br /> <br /> Given the heavy focus on this, I have to wonder if the British are being controlled by Matthew Dawkin's favorite Cappadocian NPC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-17-2025, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}